#: ../../hardware/controllers/denon_mc7000.md:94
msgid ""
"Enabling jogwheel acceleration will increase the scratch speed in proportion"
" to the physical speed at which the platters are turned, similar to Serato. "
"The precise formula for computing the scratch speed {math}`S` from the "
"physical platter ticks {math}`t` turned is as follows:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/denon_mc7000.md:96
msgid ""
"   S = \\underbrace{st \\vphantom{|}}_{\\text{base speed}} \\cdot "
"\\underbrace{c \\cdot |st|^x}_{\\text{acceleration factor}}\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/denon_mc7000.md:100
msgid "where"
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/denon_mc7000.md:102
msgid "{math}`s` is the jogwheel sensitivity"
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/denon_mc7000.md:103
msgid "{math}`t` is the number of physical platter ticks turned"
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/denon_mc7000.md:104
msgid "{math}`c` is the acceleration coefficient"
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/denon_mc7000.md:105
msgid "{math}`x` is the acceleration exponent"
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/denon_mc7000.md:108
msgid ""
"Be aware that the absolute track position will drift relative to the "
"jogwheel position when enabling jogwheel acceleration! While this is "
"convenient for scrubbing, this may make it less suitable for precise "
"scratching."
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/denon_mc7000.md:112
msgid ""
"An acceleration exponent {math}`x` of 0 and a coefficient {math}`c` of 1 are"
" equivalent to no acceleration."
msgstr ""

