msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/denon_mc7000.md:502
msgid "Hot Cue Mode (blue LED)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/denon_mc7000.md:504
msgid "8 Hot Cue positions can be defined in this mode."
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/denon_mc7000.md:0
msgid "Press one of the pad buttons to set or play a Hot Cue."
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/denon_mc7000.md:0
msgid "Use {hwlabel}`SHIFT` + pad button to delete an existing Hot Cue."
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/denon_mc7000.md:0
msgid ""
"If {hwlabel}`SLIP` is active then press and hold a pad button to play from "
"the Hot Cue position. After releasing the Hot Cue button the track continues"
" as it had been playing forward the whole time."
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/denon_mc7000.md:0
msgid ""
"Slip mode stays enabled so you can continue with more actions in slip mode."
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/denon_mc7000.md:513
msgid "Denon MC7000 CUE Mode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/denon_mc7000.md:519
msgid "Roll Mode (turquoise LED)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/denon_mc7000.md:0
msgid ""
"This mode lets you repeat a number of beats while keep pushing a pad button "
"down."
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/denon_mc7000.md:0
msgid ""
"The {hwlabel}`SLIP` function remains active so that the track continues at "
"the position where it had been playing forward the whole time."
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/denon_mc7000.md:526
msgid "Denon MC7000 ROLL Mode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/denon_mc7000.md:532
msgid "Fixed Loop Mode (yellow LED)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/denon_mc7000.md:0
msgid "This mode lets you set a dedicated loop from current position."
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/denon_mc7000.md:0
msgid "Another push on the pad button will turn the loop off."
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/denon_mc7000.md:539
msgid "Denon MC7000 FIXED LOOP Mode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/denon_mc7000.md:546
msgid "Beatjump Mode (red LED)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/denon_mc7000.md:548
msgid ""
"This mode lets you jump a number of beats while pushing a pad button once."
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/denon_mc7000.md:550
msgid "Denon MC7000 BEATJUMP Mode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/denon_mc7000.md:0
msgid ""
"Press and hold \"{hwlabel}`SHIFT`\" and then push a pad button to jump even "
"more beats."
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/denon_mc7000.md:0
msgid ""
"16, 32, 64 and 128 forward on the upper row and backwards on the lower row."
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/denon_mc7000.md:562
msgid ""
"If experimental features were set to _true_ in the {ref}`JavaScript "
"file<denon_mc7000_uservariables>` then the pad LEDs counting the beat "
"**after** the main CUE point."
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/denon_mc7000.md:564
msgid "Sampler Mode (pink LED)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/denon_mc7000.md:566
#: ../../hardware/controllers/denon_mc7000.md:592
msgid ""
"As default 16 samplers can be used. 8 samplers can be triggered from Deck 1 "
"and Deck 3 and 8 samplers can be triggered from Deck 2 and Deck 4. Deck 1 "
"will play sampler 1 to 8, Deck 2 will play sampler 9 to 16, Deck 3 will play"
" sampler 1 to 8 and Deck 4 will play sampler 9 to 16."
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/denon_mc7000.md:0
msgid "Add samplers to the sampler bank pushing a pad button."
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/denon_mc7000.md:0
msgid ""
"If a sampler is loaded, then another push on the pad button will play the "
"sampler from its Cue point."
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/denon_mc7000.md:0
msgid ""
"Push the pad button again while playing will replay the sampler from Cue "
"point."
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/denon_mc7000.md:0
msgid ""
"When a sampler is started while another one is still playing, then the "
"initial sampler stops and only the newly triggered sampler plays (single "
"play)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/denon_mc7000.md:576
#: ../../hardware/controllers/denon_mc7000.md:602
msgid ""
"Use {hwlabel}`SHIFT` + pad button to stop a sampler while playing or eject a"
" sampler when stopped."
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/denon_mc7000.md:578
msgid "Denon MC7000 SAMPLER Mode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/denon_mc7000.md:584
#: ../../hardware/controllers/denon_mc7000.md:610
msgid ""
"To use default Mixxx behaviour and allow playing multiple samplers at the "
"same time you can set the user variable ``MC7000.prevSamplerStop`` inside "
"the {ref}`JavaScript file<denon_mc7000_uservariables>` to ``false``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/denon_mc7000.md:586
msgid "Velocity Sampler Mode (purple LED)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/denon_mc7000.md:588
msgid ""
"Velocity Sampler Mode is a mode where the velocity of the push on the pad "
"determines the volume of the sampler played. A gentle push results in low "
"volume and a powerful push restults in high volume. Apart from that the "
"behavior is equal to Sampler Mode."
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/denon_mc7000.md:604
msgid "Denon MC7000 VELOCITY SAMPLER Mode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/denon_mc7000.md:612
msgid "Pitch Play Mode (green LED)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/denon_mc7000.md:614
msgid ""
"Pitch Play Mode is a mode where the pad position determines the pitch of the"
" deck played. After activating the Pitch, the pads light up in hotcue "
"colors, waiting for a selection of existing hotcue for Pitch Play or "
"creating a new hotcue at the current position. When a hotcue has been "
"selected or created, this hotcue is used for Pitch Play."
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/denon_mc7000.md:618
msgid ""
"During Pitch Play the range of pitch can be changed up or down using the "
"param buttons."
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/denon_mc7000.md:0
msgid "start Pitch Play pushing a pad button after hotcue selection."
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/denon_mc7000.md:0
msgid ""
"If the deck is playing, then another push on the pad button will start to "
"play the deck with the assigned pitch from its Cue point."
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/denon_mc7000.md:0
msgid "To reset pitch press shift and pad button."
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/denon_mc7000.md:628
msgid "Denon MC7000 PITCH PLAY Mode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/denon_mc7000.md:636
msgid "LEDs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/denon_mc7000.md:638
msgid ""
"The Channel Volume Meters matches to the ones shown in Mixxx GUI. Only when "
"clipping the red LED illuminates."
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/denon_mc7000.md:640
msgid ""
"The {hwlabel}`MASTER LEVEL` meter is not correlated to Mixxx GUI as the "
"controller handles that in Hardware."
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/denon_mc7000.md:642
msgid ""
"Button LEDs are fully mapped for the first function. As you press and hold "
"{hwlabel}`SHIFT` then the secondary functions have only got some flashing "
"LEDs mapped, e.g. TAP and KEY SYNC, when activated."
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/denon_mc7000.md:644
msgid ""
"Press {hwlabel}`SHIFT` + {hwlabel}`Deck` to switch Platter Ring LED Mode."
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/denon_mc7000.md:646
msgid "Mode 0 - Single 'off' LED chase (all other LEDs are 'on')"
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/denon_mc7000.md:647
msgid "Mode 1 - Single 'on' LED chase (all other LEDs are 'off')"
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/denon_mc7000.md:650
msgid ""
"The default mode can be set to ``0`` or ``1`` inside the {ref}`JavaScript "
"file<denon_mc7000_uservariables>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/denon_mc7000.md:652
msgid "Platter Ring LEDs are correlated with the {hwlabel}`VINYL` button."
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/denon_mc7000.md:654
msgid ""
"If vinyl mode is enabled, the LED imitates a turntable platter spinning at "
"33.3 rpm."
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/denon_mc7000.md:655
msgid ""
"If vinyl mode is disabled, the current track position is indicated by the "
"Platter LEDs starting at the top."
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/denon_mc7000.md:658
msgid ""
"The Platter Ring LEDs are not moving while the track position is 'negative'."
" That means if the position is before the track starts then the position LED"
" keeps staying at most up position."
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/denon_mc7000.md:660
msgid "Known Issues"
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/denon_mc7000.md:662
msgid ""
"Some Performance Pad modes are not available (Cue Loop, Flip, Slicer Loop)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/denon_mc7000.md:663
msgid "The Effect Units don't use Mixxx' Standard Effects Mapping"
msgstr ""
